  "$comment": "Football (soccer) leagues, one per tab inside the ⚽ tab. Add one by appending an entry — nothing in the model or API hardcodes these ids. `openfootball` is the primary results source (JSON, current through the latest season, and it carries HALF-TIME scores); `footballData` supplies historical 1X2 closing odds, which is what lets the model be measured against the market; `footballcsv` is the older mirror kept as a fallback for seasons openfootball does not have; `oddsSportKeys` are The Odds API keys for upcoming fixtures. `tier` 2 marks a second division: it is ingested so PROMOTED clubs have a rating (a fixture against one otherwise gets no model at all), and the cross-division offset is measured per country — see docs/FOOTBALL.md.",
